// AuraLead AI data model (plan §5). SQLite is the source of truth; Prisma 7 with the
// better-sqlite3 driver adapter (ADR-02). The datasource URL lives in prisma.config.ts.
//
// Conventions (plan §5):
// - IDs are cuid2 strings. Money is BigInt paise (`*Paise`, ADR-07). Rates are Int basis points.
// - Every tenant-owned model carries `workspaceId` and an index (or unique) that starts with it
//   (E10, ADR-42; enforced by tests/unit/arch/tenant-columns.test.ts). It is nullable only on
//   system rows (Job, JobAttempt, AuditEvent, WebhookEvent, WebhookRejection, Invite).
// - Child -> parent references inside a tenant use composite foreign keys
//   (workspaceId, parentId) -> parent(workspaceId, id), backed by @@unique([workspaceId, id]) on the
//   parent, so the database itself rejects a cross-workspace reference (ADR-47).
// - Partial unique indexes use the `partialIndexes` preview feature (`where: raw(...)`), so
//   `prisma migrate dev` knows about them and never drops them as drift. Each one is marked
//   `-- PARTIAL UNIQUE` in the migration SQL (ADR-47).
// - JSON columns are never filtered on; filterable data gets real columns.

generator client {
  provider        = "prisma-client"
  output          = "../src/generated/prisma"
  previewFeatures = ["partialIndexes"]
}

datasource db {
  provider = "sqlite"
}

